  ATTEMPT.md sec3.1's actual (20b,inf) row for cell '100,1000' (=cell A) is
  '-9.7% (z=-9.4)', n=34.1M -- NOT literally '-9.66%'.
  The literal string '9.66' appears exactly once elsewhere tied to a %
  figure in the whole archive: short_cycle_dynamics_attempt/adversarial/
  REFEREE_REPORT.md line 256 / adv_reduction.log line 43, for cell
  'b=400,c=100' (= this front's OWN cell B, not cell A!), comparing
  measured full-phi against phi_REDC_full (Claim 4's refuted reduction
  formula) -- a DIFFERENT quantity from a DIFFERENT test (sec3.2, not the
  sec4.1 (20b,inf) far-tail-vs-phi_U(c'') table T1 actually reuses).
  CONCLUSION: '-9.66%' is a genuine mis-citation (wrong cell AND wrong
  quantity), coincidentally close in VALUE to the correct cell-A figure
  (-9.7%), so it does not flip cell A's classification, but the framing
  '2.52/9.66=26%, well under 1/3' is reference-choice-fragile: using the
  low end of the front's OWN pre-registered confirmed range for cell A
